 HTTP paths did not fail and its success path returns 0; the reported exit 1 is not attributable to Gerrit (most likely the calling shell; unrecoverable).\nFix (commit 5a4efd52a39): every post-vote exception path now reconciles. Submit non-409 HTTPError / URLError / OSError / ValueError -> re-read ?o=ALL_REVISIONS; MERGED with the submitted revision among its patch sets -> print merged, exit 0; else print error + Gerrit body, exit 1; failed re-read -> exit 1 naming both errors. Hashtag POST failures only warn. 409 path unchanged. RED first: the 7 new tests failed on the pre-fix script while the 25 existing tests passed; after the fix 32/32 pass. Lint (ratchets) and typecheck clean. make verify running.","timestamp":1794464047951806621},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Commit 5a4efd52a39: make verify exit 0 on 2026-11-11 22:13-23:15 PST (21132 passed, 29 skipped; integration 218 passed, 2 skipped). Pushed as Gerrit 3361; awaiting LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1794467831116846001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence: Gerrit 3361 merged at revision 5a4efd52a39f59f5bf2e65bc6e51d0cceed05a6a (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved), submitted 2026-11-11 23:42 PST with scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py from the fix itself (exit 0). AC1: request trail recorded in the earlier comment. AC2-AC5: tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py, 7 new tests (RED 7 failed before the fix, 32/32 after); the 409 tests are untouched. AC6: make verify exit 0, 22:13-23:15 PST, on 5a4efd52a39.","timestamp":1794469432380088001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 23:52 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED (class preexisting). Gerrit 3361 merged at 5a4efd52a39; completion gate passed. Nothing pending on this ticket. Worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-milksnake can be removed.","timestamp":1794469940141126001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794370756550300379,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8804cd8d-4931-4c42-bf09-ea391bf3aca6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"95bd-beb1-8c3f-465f"},{"link_uuid":"84afee57-10e5-4dbe-9874-01eec1d19a14","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6dd0-9a39-0ff1-4b13"},{"link_uuid":"07bf2a49-6d93-4b1b-a638-2f9c6c9f6ae6","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"8b1c-c577-366b-47d5"}],"description":"## Observation\n\nOn 2026-11-10 ~19:55 PST `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3344 --revision <sha>` reportedly exited 1, yet change 3344 is MERGED (merge commit 9f8b2af21c8 on origin/main). The script's stderr was not captured.\n\n## Root-cause evidence (read-only, Gerrit `httpd_log` on i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\nThat invocation made exactly 3 requests, all `Python-urllib/3.12` from the same client, all HTTP 200:\n- 03:55:04.357Z `GET /a/changes/3344?o=CURRENT_REVISION&o=DETAILED_LABELS&o=SUBMITTABLE` 200\n- 03:55:04.653Z `POST /a/changes/3344/hashtags` 200\n- 03:55:05.109Z `POST /a/changes/3344/revisions/7a3baab7a2c6.../submit` 200 (Gerrit rebased and merged)\n\nSo none of the script's HTTP paths failed, and no request timed out. On the success path the script returns 0, so the reported exit 1 is not attributable to a Gerrit response; it most likely came from the calling shell, which no evidence recovers. The script still has a real defect the ticket names: any exception after the vote check (a non-409 `HTTPError`, a `URLError`/timeout, or an unparseable body from the hashtag or submit request) escapes as a traceback with exit 1, even when Gerrit has already merged the change. This plan fixes that class for every such path.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py`:\n1. The session-hashtag POST becomes best-effort: any `HTTPError`, `URLError`, `OSError` or `ValueError` prints a warning naming the error and continues to the submit (a missing ownership tag must not block or misreport a submit).\n2. The submit POST catches `HTTPError` (non-409), `URLError`, `OSError` (timeouts) and `ValueError` (unparseable body). It then re-reads the change with all revisions: if `status` is `MERGED` and the requested revision is one of the change's revisions, it prints `submitted: change <n> merged (revision <sha>)` and returns 0; otherwise it prints the original error and Gerrit's response body (for an `HTTPError`) and returns 1. A failure of that re-read is reported with the original error and returns 1. The 409 path is unchanged (exit 2).\n3. The module docstring's exit-code table documents exit 1 as \"the submit failed and the change is not merged\" and drops \"re-raises\".\nNo new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests with a stubbed `_request` (same style as the existing tests):\n- submit raises non-409 `HTTPError` (502) but the re-read shows MERGED with the revision → exit 0, prints \"merged\";\n- submit raises `URLError` (timeout) but MERGED → exit 0;\n- submit returns an unparseable body (`ValueError`) but MERGED → exit 0;\n- submit raises 502 and the re-read shows NEW → exit 1, stderr has Gerrit's body;\n- submit raises `URLError` and the re-read itself fails → exit 1 naming both;\n- hashtag POST raises 500 → warning on stderr, submit still runs, exit 0;\n- the existing 409 tests pass unchanged; the existing `test_safe_submit_reraises_non_409_submit_http_error` is replaced by the not-merged exit-1 test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] The 3344 incident's request trail is recorded on this ticket (3 requests, all 200), showing the script's own HTTP calls did not fail.\n  provenance: environment=production Gerrit host i-00880b2c7f13527c5 httpd_log via SSM; principal=frontier AWS profile; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read-only grep of the request log\n- [x] Every exception path after the vote check (hashtag POST, submit POST: non-409 HTTPError, URLError/timeout, unparseable body) has a unit test.\n- [x] A submit that raises after Gerrit merged the requested revision exits 0 and prints that it merged.\n- [x] A submit that fails without merging exits 1 and prints Gerrit's response body.\n- [x] The 409 path's behaviour and tests are unchanged.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-milksnake worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py","reason":"reconcile post-vote errors"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py","reason":"per-path tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6dd0-9a39-0ff1-4b13"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4f70ef2f-2687-4b90-a065-97079c430e6f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd1a-4c91-151f-4e1d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"gerrit_safe_submit.py exits 1 although Gerrit merged the change","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7e577768-f11a-4993-aed5-732757450496","09167714-9b0f-4897-9a30-70d737a864b6","3dc12184-b2ea-4a05-9490-a85877c05fce","c6bde8f6-7b58-4f03-ac4f-89159278bee7","b1688e96-3041-45d2-9d72-168eebf0904d","0ebeb605-75fd-42f9-b026-ddb2f0c0e515","f8908f03-a3fe-4c88-9136-e7bebc295dc8","84afee57-10e5-4dbe-9874-01eec1d19a14","5dc9d0f7-262a-4d0c-b761-ddf4e5d9de1d","bf4ae598-c9b8-4f9b-a34c-580c6a6d9ed0","4f70ef2f-2687-4b90-a065-97079c430e6f","29bbee43-d117-4786-a188-853fa823ec21","07bf2a49-6d93-4b1b-a638-2f9c6c9f6ae6","83d3d931-df31-406c-bd7f-ef622930a025"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794469940141126002,"uuid":"156a868c-6a87-4c49-bd9c-0b98080b3b2f"}